00:00:57.760 --> 00:01:01.149
Careful for spoilers if you don't know
anything, but Cue The Dragons,

00:01:01.149 --> 00:01:05.030
Let's GO! In the pre-roll The Forge is
being used to melt down Ned Stark's giant

00:01:05.030 --> 00:01:07.060
two-handed Valyrian Great Sword (ICE).

00:01:07.060 --> 00:01:10.390
It's being made into two smaller blades.
The larger one on the left is Oathkeeper.

00:01:10.390 --> 00:01:14.460
And the smaller one on the right is Widow's
Wail. #2 - This is the new home where

00:01:14.460 --> 00:01:16.820
Daenerys' dragons live beneath HER new
home.

00:01:16.820 --> 00:01:20.240
There's actually a screenshot of that building
later in this video that I'll include.

00:01:20.240 --> 00:01:23.270
Remember that last shot of Drogon in the
video? Yeah he's big!

00:01:23.270 --> 00:01:26.390
#3 - Joffrey plays with one of "said new
blades." (Widow's Wail)

00:01:26.390 --> 00:01:30.369
#4 - Arya gets back something she lost at
The Crossroads.

00:01:30.369 --> 00:01:34.440
#5 - Bronn teaches Jaime to learn to fight
with his left hand.

00:01:34.440 --> 00:01:37.950
#6 - Brann tries to communicate with the Three-Eyed Crow.

00:01:37.950 --> 00:01:42.390
#7 - This is the first good shot of the
new actor playing Daario (Michiel Huisman)

00:01:42.390 --> 00:01:46.190
#8 - This is the red Viper and his lover
Ellaria Sand.

00:01:46.190 --> 00:01:50.619
We didn't see her in the Season 4
Trailer. #9 - The Hound at The Crossroads in

00:01:50.619 --> 00:01:51.399
the same scene

00:01:51.399 --> 00:01:54.929
Arya was in previously. --- So this is where
we get to the actor interviews. I'm

00:01:54.929 --> 00:01:55.849
actually going to skip

00:01:55.849 --> 00:01:58.709
a lot of the things they say unless they
have really important clues about

00:01:58.709 --> 00:01:59.369
what's coming,

00:01:59.369 --> 00:02:02.789
or important details about things they
changed from the books. But continuing on!

00:02:02.789 --> 00:02:06.700
#10 - Gwendoline Christie the actually highlights a really important thing.

00:02:06.700 --> 00:02:10.020
That some of the actors read ahead in
the books and some do not.

00:02:10.020 --> 00:02:10.759
She obviously did,

00:02:10.759 --> 00:02:13.959
but a good example of someone who does
not pay attention to the books is

00:02:13.959 --> 00:02:14.590
Peter Dinklage.

00:02:14.590 --> 00:02:17.510
The ones that don't mostly just do it
out of concern that it will hurt their

00:02:17.510 --> 00:02:20.780
performance for some really important
scenes, like the wedding to Sansa

00:02:20.780 --> 00:02:24.720
or all the big action set pieces this
season.  #11 - David Benioff

00:02:24.720 --> 00:02:28.020
actually say something really important
here, that some of the biggest scenes

00:02:28.020 --> 00:02:29.500
come at the END of the season.

00:02:29.500 --> 00:02:32.680
We can talk more about the timeline
in on of my future videos maybe.

00:02:32.680 --> 00:02:37.100
#12 - Remember at the end of Season 3 Sansa did not know about the Red Wedding.

00:02:37.100 --> 00:02:40.500
#13 - if you look at this slate it says
"Episode 6".

00:02:40.500 --> 00:02:44.410
In the background you can see the Red
Viper, Tywin and Mace Tyrell.

00:02:44.410 --> 00:02:47.860
He's kind of fuzzy though. They're the
people presiding over Tyrion's Trial.

00:02:47.860 --> 00:02:51.460
This is actually pretty huge, so  we can all
adjust our timelines accordingly.

00:02:51.460 --> 00:02:54.670
#14 - Even though Cersei and Tyrion really
hate each other,

00:02:54.670 --> 00:02:58.170
Lena Headey and Peter Dinklage used to
share flat in Dubrovnik whenever they

00:02:58.170 --> 00:02:58.860
were filming.

00:02:58.860 --> 00:03:02.670
They're actually really good friends in
real life. #15 - Tyrion and Jaime spend a

00:03:02.670 --> 00:03:03.940
lot of time together.

00:03:03.940 --> 00:03:07.720
It's like the season of brotherly love...No,
not THAT "Twincest" kind of love...

00:03:07.720 --> 00:03:11.630
#16 - This is the first on set interview
with Pedro Pascal

00:03:11.630 --> 00:03:14.840
HBO has posted. He hasn't officially said a
lot about himself

00:03:14.840 --> 00:03:18.020
as the Red Viper before this. #17 - More
Slates.

00:03:18.020 --> 00:03:22.770
So this says from "Episode 5". In the next
slide you can actually see Cersei in black.

00:03:22.770 --> 00:03:25.810
So we can probably adjust our timelines
just a little bit more.

00:03:25.810 --> 00:03:28.730
I hope you're getting excited because it seems like big events are getting pushed

00:03:28.730 --> 00:03:30.610
forward and forward and foward in the season!

00:03:30.610 --> 00:03:34.650
#18 Rory McCann can actually starts all the
Joffrey Roast clips that the actors filmed

00:03:34.650 --> 00:03:37.480
for that promotional stunt HBO did
earlier this year.

00:03:37.480 --> 00:03:41.040
It was Maisie Williams and a few the
other actors making fun of Joffrey.

00:03:41.040 --> 00:03:44.840
#19 - This is a much better shot the Royal
Wedding Feast.

00:03:44.840 --> 00:03:48.970
#20 - The scene that they talk about the
takes up half the episode is most likely

00:03:48.970 --> 00:03:49.720
the banquet

00:03:49.720 --> 00:03:52.750
and the wedding combined. Look at all
those extras.

00:03:52.750 --> 00:03:56.100
It's the biggest scene that they've
filmed since the Season 1 Premiere.

00:03:56.100 --> 00:03:59.120
#21 - The actors talk about how amazing the
sets are.

00:03:59.120 --> 00:04:02.390
The art designer Deborah Riley got a new
featurette that HBO did earlier

00:04:02.390 --> 00:04:02.950
this year,

00:04:02.950 --> 00:04:06.000
and the Art Designer Gemma Jackson from Season 3 won an

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:09.190
Art Directors Guild Award for their work
during that Season. They have some the

00:04:09.190 --> 00:04:10.080
the best sets of

00:04:10.080 --> 00:04:14.200
any show on television right now.  #22 - The
evolution of the Dragons.

00:04:14.200 --> 00:04:17.340
This is one thing that I'm MOST excited
about in Season 4.

00:04:17.340 --> 00:04:20.639
David Benioff talks about the challenges
that come with controlling the Dragons

00:04:20.639 --> 00:04:22.199
once they become really big.

00:04:22.199 --> 00:04:25.699
#23 - This is a good shot of the library of
the Night's Watch.

00:04:25.699 --> 00:04:29.180
Or as close a thing as they have to it.
There are actually texts in there that

00:04:29.180 --> 00:04:30.910
predate the creation of the wall.

00:04:30.910 --> 00:04:33.430
I always thought that everything they
needed to win against the White Walkers

00:04:33.430 --> 00:04:34.690
were in those books.

00:04:34.690 --> 00:04:37.980
But because Sam is the only one who reads
them, the chances of them

00:04:37.980 --> 00:04:41.550
finding that critical information is
really slim.

00:04:41.550 --> 00:04:44.510
#24 - I just love that Gwendoline Christie is
almost giggling her way through

00:04:44.510 --> 00:04:45.300
explaining this

00:04:45.300 --> 00:04:49.820
really violent think Brienne has to do to
defend herrself. What a lovable goofball :)

00:04:49.820 --> 00:04:53.120
#25 - DB Weiss actually says something
really good here.

00:04:53.120 --> 00:04:56.600
While the Red Wedding represented this
epic set piece for Season 3,

00:04:56.600 --> 00:04:59.930
Season 4 has several scenes that are
on that scale.

00:04:59.930 --> 00:05:03.490
#26 - This is a really good external shot of Mereen.

00:05:03.490 --> 00:05:06.780
#27 - Jamie unveils Brienne's new armor. She's actually wearing it during

00:05:06.780 --> 00:05:07.690
this interview.

00:05:07.690 --> 00:05:10.790
And finally, #28 - Let's leave it on Drogon.

00:05:10.790 --> 00:05:14.300
Look at how much bigger he's gotten. He's
the biggest to the 3 and it becomes

00:05:14.300 --> 00:05:17.690
a huge issue in Season 4 for Dany...He
looks hungry,

00:05:17.690 --> 00:05:20.830
better watch out! So this was a lot of fun
again, but there is one more thing that I

00:05:20.830 --> 00:05:22.480
want to add. Maisie Williams said

00:05:22.480 --> 00:05:26.050
the good guys are coming back, but that
was a bit misleading. The subtext is is

00:05:26.050 --> 00:05:28.949
that EVERYONE gets dumped on this Season. The good guys AND the bad.

00:05:28.949 --> 00:05:32.070
And technically no one is either
really good or really bad. It's all

00:05:32.070 --> 00:05:32.880
shades of gray.

00:05:32.880 --> 00:05:35.930
Unless you are Ramsay Snow. That guy's just plain evil!

